# SFT execution status v0.85

2026-09-13. The local guardian/bootstrap/rootfs/entry composition is implemented
and synthetic-tested. This completes the local composition-code part of the
existing Gate 5 import task; Gate 5 itself is not complete. No new roadmap gate
has been introduced.

## Completed in this successor

- Rootfs adapter v1 (24 tests) binds/seals the software root before input/output
  mounts, re-pins the root in the final namespace, pivots without another root
  bind and checks that the input/output views survive.
- Bootstrap v2 (24 tests) composes that adapter with the existing cgroup,
  network, Landlock, IPC, authority-descriptor and privilege-drop controls.
  The exact entry and three environment pins are fixed.
- Guardian composition v2 (30 tests) binds the parent's generation nonce, arms
  controller/deadline supervision before one release, checks the closed entry
  report and mounted-input totals, and requires successful exits, EOF and
  removal of its empty owned cgroup.
- Prepared entry v1 (30 tests) verifies the helper/source/control bundle before
  one tiny coordinator call. It retains only fixed statuses, hashes and counts.

All 108 new tests plus the previous 87 component tests pass on Python 3.11.15 and
3.13.7: 195 tests per runtime, no failures, errors or skips. Final test processes
had audit hooks denying network/process/native-library calls and ML imports;
no prohibited operation was attempted and no ML root was loaded. Eight new
Python files pass syntax and 100-column checks. No Ruff or native Linux result
is claimed.

## Integration fixes made before handoff

The ordinary frozen lumi package initializer may load model libraries too early
for the new runner's pre-ML check. The authenticated entry now establishes an
inert exact lumi namespace first; original source bytes are not changed.

Review also found that /outputs/attempt-001 gives a parent path too shallow for
the frozen runner. The entry now exclusively creates /outputs/import (0700,
worker-owned) and uses /outputs/import/attempt-001. A regression test executes
the actual frozen path validator, not a replacement validator.

The entry's generated success report is tested against the actual new guardian
parser/validator. Existing sources, previous evidence and existing CI are
unchanged. All new files are still local; nothing was committed or pushed.

## Remaining existing sequence

1. Prepare this successor's nonce-bound tiny generated fixture, root-owned
   worker-readable controls, authenticated source manifest and rootfs scaffold.
2. Bind a verified Linux x86_64 CPython 3.12 launcher and run the bounded
   generated-only native qualification of this composition.
3. Separately admit the dedicated host/runtime, input backing-store and writer
   exclusion, full-size resource limits and real-host readback, then perform
   the authorized real checkpoint CPU import.
4. After successful verified import, complete the existing GPU-worker,
   private-data and CUDA-smoke prerequisites before SFT.

The tiny successor keeps the existing 4 GiB outer cgroup and 90-second bound;
its coordinator is limited to 60 seconds, 64 MiB logical reads and 16 MiB
import writes. Source-copy writes are a separate maximum 4 MiB. The 512 MiB
tmpfs and 64 MiB shm values are capacities, not cumulative write counters.
These are not full-size host admission or measured resource requirements.

No new rootfs/tensor fixture was prepared or executed here. Source origin,
external-writer exclusion and real host capacity remain parent prerequisites.
Read-only mounts and synthetic test results are not an authorization to import
the real checkpoint. The public real import entry still rejects
host_guard_not_bound.

No real checkpoint/tokenizer/dataset payload, network/S3/instance, GPU, inference
or training operation occurred. GPU is not needed for the next preparation-code
step. Execution permission, training authorization and production eligibility
remain false.

